{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Sword:</b> when it is in its sheath it is closed, therefore [Scripture says] \"they have opened.\" Some say that the opening of a sword is the brandishing; comparable is \"and they are openings\" [Genesis 26:15]. Now behold: the sword is in the open, and the bow is in secret."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:55.955708837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}